course: dictionary
lesson: 14972
title: Formal words for paid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Remunerated is a formal word that means paid. You will see it in job adverts, contracts and exams. In everyday talk, people usually say paid.
explain: «The nurses were well remunerated for working through the night.» The word well is the clue. Well remunerated means well paid, because the nurses were paid for their work and the pay was good.
explain: Use the swap check. Put paid in place of remunerated: «The nurses were well paid for working through the night.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Remunerate is the verb, and remunerated is its past form, so it means was or were paid. «The school will remunerate the volunteers for their time» means the school will pay the volunteers for their time.
fact: Remunerated means paid for work.
fact: To remunerate someone is to pay them for work or a service.
fact: «Well remunerated» means well paid.
fact: «Remunerated work» means work that people are paid for.
fact: Remunerated is a formal word, used in contracts, job adverts and exams. In everyday talk, people say paid.
exercise: «The gardeners were remunerated for clearing the park.» What does remunerated mean? | *Paid for work | Given a prize for winning | Asked to stop working | Thrown out of the park
exercise: Which everyday word means the same as remunerated? | Parked | Hurried | Packed | *Paid
exercise: «The job is well remunerated, so many people apply.» What does well remunerated suggest? | The job is dull | *The pay is good | Nobody is hired | The work is outdoors
test: «Mia was remunerated for every hour she spent tutoring.» What does remunerated mean here? | Given a holiday | Sent home early | *Paid for her work | Tired from her work
test: What does it mean to remunerate someone? | To teach someone a new skill | *To pay someone for work | To thank someone with words | To hire someone for a single day
exam: Which everyday word could replace remunerated in «The workers were remunerated fairly»? | *Paid | Painted | Parted | Pressed
